I think these are both true.  ;-)

Matt was saying this morning that what he finds particularly interesting in the
Major trophies is the different playing styles they showcase and how (to name
four in particular) marvin, rast, aardvark and eit_brad are all clearly experts
at playing the same _game_ but in such vastly different ways.

Personally, I'm also pleased to see the Major trophies spread out among
multiple players since that demonstrates that there are other expert players
out there than marvin.  He has a clear lead at the moment, but at the very
least sawtooth and aardvark (and probably rast and a few others) are improving
to the point that they should be strong contenders at the very top in the next
few years.

One of the goals of the Challenge trophies is to be able to add new in-game
and/or NetHack-related material which lets folks who aren't as clearly in that
top-tier also have a competitive opportunity.  Since the Challenge content will
be ne to most players, the competitive field is a bit more level for them.  And
they can be bypassed or ignored, so the folks who _are_ competitive for the
Major and Minor trophies can choose not to have the Challenges affect their
competition for those trophies.

The Clan trophies could also contribute to this, though we need to diversify
them a bit to really get some of this benefit from them.

